From: Alejandro Pacheco <alepacheco99@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:56:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 60/90] Check reply length before V4 reply check

In init_creds_validate_reply(), a reply that is not a KRB-ERROR or
AS-REP is examined for a Kerberos 4 error header by checking the first
two bytes.  A one-byte reply causes a read past the end of the buffer.
Reject replies shorter than two bytes as the wrong message type before
looking at the second byte.

Add a test program which feeds short and unrecognized replies to
krb5_init_creds_step().

[ghudson@mit.edu: updated notice.rst/NOTICE for test program license]

